● The plan for #3 is posted as a comment on the issue:
  https://github.com/Wutru03/ADD-kentekenQuiz/issues/3#issuecomment-6631123614.
  I changed no repo files and built nothing. I'm waiting for your go.

  What the plan does: Submit scores the guesses in a new pure file,
  src/lib/scoring.ts, and saves one row in a wide rounds table. It then replaces
  the guess screen with a result screen that reads that round back by id. The
  comment lists every file, the table columns and the task list. The task list
  ends with the Expo Go tests.

  My recommendation for each question:
  1. Coordinates: pass latitude and longitude as route params next to vehicle.
     Keep "Guess the stats" disabled until the location has resolved, either to
     a position or to null. I'd also add a 10 second cap in getCurrentCoords,
     since it has no timeout today.
  2. Play again: split Play into an outer screen and an inner PlayForm with a
     key taken from a route param. "Play again" calls router.dismissTo with a
     fresh key, which remounts the form empty. I haven't run this, so I still
     have to confirm dismissTo applies the new param.
  3. Double tap and Try again: disable Submit while the save is pending and
     check a useRef flag. Once the save succeeds the guess screen is gone, so
     Submit can't be tapped again. A failed insert leaves no row, so Try again
     can't duplicate.
  4. Restart check: the result screen shows "Round #id saved". After you kill
     Expo Go, the next round should get the next number, not #1. This needs no
     extra queries.
  5. Shared button: yes. Create src/components/button.tsx and use it in Play,
     Guess, the result screen and error-view.tsx. The error-view.tsx swap is the
     one edit outside the files you listed.
  6. Spec gap I found: if no stat can be asked for a vehicle, Submit is enabled
     with nothing to score. I'd keep Submit disabled in that case.

  git status still shows the cleanup uncommitted (8 files), and I left it alone.
  AGENTS.md is one of those files, with a deleted expo-env.d.ts line. My later
  AGENTS.md edit will land on top of that, so commit the cleanup first if you
  want closes #3 to stay clean.

